WHAT IS FUSED (in-memory module swap; no MACE/e3nn source edits)
  model.spherical_harmonics (e3nn SphericalHarmonics lmax=3, normalize=True, 'component') -> FusedSphericalHarmonics
      fwd kernel fe_sh_fwd   : vectors[E,3] -> edge_attrs[E,16] (F.normalize eps=1e-12 semantics, e3nn order/sign, sqrt(2l+1))
      bwd kernel fe_sh_bwd   : analytic d/dvectors incl. (I-uu^T)/|v| projection
  model.radial_embedding (RadialEmbeddingBlock: BesselBasis(8, r_max 5) x PolynomialCutoff(p=5), no distance transform)
      -> FusedRadialEmbedding, returns (edge_feats[E,8], None) exactly like stock (cutoff=None)
      fwd kernel fe_radial_fwd: lengths[E,1] -> prefactor*sin(w r)/r * envelope(r)*(r<r_max)
      bwd kernel fe_radial_bwd: d/dlengths
  Launches: SH+radial was 54 kernels fwd / 168 fwd+bwd (incl. norm) -> 2 fwd + 2 bwd own kernels (3 fwd / 10 fwd+bwd incl.
  the stock norm + autograd accumulation). Two independent modules: no cache/handoff between them -> nothing can go stale
  across calls or graph replays. Not fused: get_edge_vectors_and_lengths (gather/sub/norm in prepare_graph, a plain
  function, not a module) stays stock; grads flow to positions/displacement through it, so stress works.
  install() raises NotImplementedError on any other SH/radial config (lmax, normalization, basis type, distance transform,
  apply_cutoff=False, trainable Bessel weights).
  Double backward: once_differentiable (create_graph -> grads have no grad_fn; second backward raises RuntimeError).
  Graph safety: current stream, no host syncs (host scalars read at install), output shapes depend only on E, E==0 skips launch.
  Compiled with --fmad=false, sm_90.

